-- The same made-up Licensing Act as overrides-forgotten.l4, this time with
-- section 5 honouring its own opening words: it calls the decision that
-- encodes section 3, negated, because it may trade only where section 3's
-- bar does not apply.

GIVEN metres IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 — the premises are within 100 metres of a school` metres MEANS
    metres LESS THAN 100

@ref Licensing Act s 5 — "Subject to section 3, a licensee may trade between 8am and 10pm."
GIVEN hour IS A NUMBER, metres IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5 — a licensee may trade` hour metres MEANS
        "Subject to section 3,"
    ... NOT (`s 3 — the premises are within 100 metres of a school` metres)
    ... "a licensee may trade between 8am and 10pm."
    ... hour AT LEAST 8 AND hour AT MOST 22

-- Noon, 50 metres from a school. Section 3 bars it, and now section 5 agrees.
#EVAL `s 5 — a licensee may trade` 12 50
-- Noon, 500 metres from a school. Nothing bars it.
#EVAL `s 5 — a licensee may trade` 12 500
